id: pm-github-selected-discussion-decisions
title: Capture selected GitHub discussion passages as reviewed native Decisions
description: "Own GitHub issue-comment decision capture, using native SDK persistence and source citations. Overlap rechecked: core stores Decisions and notes; pm-review imports PR reviewer findings; pm-linear captures its selected Linear threads; pm-evidence owns citation resolution. None owns explicitly marked GitHub issue-comment spans."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: changelog-unreleased,decisions,discussion,evidence
created_at: "2026-10-29T06:56:09.992Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T08:23:14.892Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Unmarked prose creates no decisions; editing a selected comment makes apply stale; repeated approved capture creates no duplicate observation; source instructions remain inert data; strict bounded inputs and outputs; model-based SDK read-back over at least 500 seeded random sequences; no-git and packed npm/Bun acceptance; exact-head CI release gates
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T06:56:44.664Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked against current core declarations and sibling sources: pm-review/src/tracker.ts owns PR findings; pm-linear/index.ts captureLinearThread owns Linear evidence notes; pm-evidence/src/evidence.ts owns citation resolution/review. This adds only selected GitHub issue-comment decisions. Plan: one explicitly marked UTF-16 span per independent native Decision, canonical source URL plus exact JSON evidence, deterministic identity, explicit parent/scope and registry-derived status; preview and apply share preparation. Re-read SDK target history and selected remote comment immediately before each create. No transaction isolation claim: ordinary writers can still race between the last read and SDK create; deterministic IDs prevent duplicate creation. No multi-step destructive compensation or frozen recovery plans."
  "2026-10-29T07:06:11.279Z",codex-agent,"Implementation now shares a strict selection/evidence/report schema across SDK and CLI. Exact quotes live as JSON data in native Decision bodies, with attributed GitHub source revision and native linked docs. Focused real non-git tests cover stale source edits, parent ABA, independent bad records, retries, preservation of edited targets and competing parent writes at every observable boundary. SDK create appends explicit-unset audit metadata to history messages; replay recognition now respects that supported suffix while retaining the full history revision guard."
  "2026-10-29T07:20:41.491Z",codex-agent,"Seeded state model passed 500 sequences (seed 0xdec1510): 1741 operations, 337 Decision creates, 162 older-input replays, 49 stale-source refusals. State is read through the SDK and compared with a second real SDK tracker, including native fields and relationships. Native semantic staging was subsequently added through previewItemMutations using the exact create producer; it catches project-specific create requirements without source writes. The model will be rerun with this final staging path before handoff. Targeted coverage currently covers every new line/function; HTTP/history boundary cases complete branch evidence next."
  "2026-10-29T07:37:10.601Z",codex-agent,"Targeted native/HTTP suite passes 12/12. Both new authored modules measure 100% statements, branches, functions and lines under targeted c8; no threshold or source exclusions changed. Tests cover peer success, malformed foreign history, custom status registries, native schema refusals, source/parent staleness, exact inert quotes and late I/O recovery. Final-read reconciliation now shares one state verdict for ordinary interleavings and ambiguous create failures. Full release checks remain delegated to unchanged npm/Bun CI gates to protect the shared host."
  "2026-10-29T07:42:15.942Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof ran in a disposable source copy: disabling only the new SDK create in captureGithubDiscussion failed the marked-span real-SDK regression; restoring it passed 1/1. The package worktree was never altered. Public snapshot fingerprints also caught command-level get usage recording, so capture now reads documents via public locateItem/readLocatedItem helpers instead of PmClient.get during planning. This preserves SDK normalization while avoiding derived usage writes in the source tracker."
  "2026-10-29T07:48:51.802Z",codex-agent,"Public data validation: a certified 158-item public tracker snapshot, five public issue comments, and 24 sampled native contexts produced 24 reviewable plans, 24 identical replays and 24 empty-selection zero plans. Largest receipts: 905 JSON bytes and 829 TOON bytes. Complete snapshot fingerprints remained identical; tracker writes 0 and remote writes 0. An additional literal read-only filesystem sample produced one bounded native_refused row due to the pinned SDK staging-mode limitation, with identical snapshot bytes and zero writes; tracked separately in pm-github-sdk-preview-readonly."
  "2026-10-29T07:50:49.179Z",codex-agent,"The initial large-population 500-sequence model passed before SDK staging was added. A later staging run was deliberately stopped after 991 seconds because copying a growing tracker at every preview was too expensive on the shared host; its interruption output is retained. The final model still runs 500 seeded random operation sequences with all native-field, relationship, older-input, CRLF and round-trip checks, but reuses a bounded population of source revisions to avoid quadratic staging copies. The final linked test run follows this change."
  "2026-10-29T08:09:21.760Z",codex-agent,"The final bounded 500-sequence model and focused native suite passed through the linked pm test command. Additional hardening now admits SDK-supported Unicode/slash-bearing status names and GitHub bot attribution, rejects coerced approval controls, and reads tombstone history even when a target document is absent. Deleted targets invalidate old approvals and are preserved rather than resurrected. Canonical native ID whitespace aliases remain delegated to the SDK; native ID characters are still constrained by the SDK itself. Final targeted cases and unchanged full CI gates verify these additions."
  "2026-10-29T08:19:46.418Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted run through the pinned pm test command passes 16/16, with zero failures/skips and 100% statements/branches/functions/lines for discussion-schema.ts and discussions.ts under c8. The earlier linked 500-sequence model run also passed. Packed acceptance on CLI 2026.10.28 passes all five launchers (project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx, native Bun bunx): each creates one Decision, repeats unchanged and reads exact evidence through the installed host. Tested archive SHA-256: 18829c1e76c6e76174f878febf864cabba590ad3189f1e1b569cd301a791a8fb. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication gate pass; package-wide npm/Bun release evidence will come from exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-29T08:23:14.892Z",codex-agent,"Local strict health reports no history drift or integrity failure, but refuses a host/extension SDK version skew (2026.10.25 versus 2026.10.28); four older in-progress records are advisory. Dependency pins remain unchanged per the queue rule. The same main base passed fresh CI run 40808490467; this PR will use fresh exact-head CI for authoritative tracker health and package-wide npm/Bun release evidence. The local warning is retained rather than hidden or repaired."
